    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19192" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gaesum</span></b> , less correctly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gēsum</span></b> , i, n.
		Celtic, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a long</i>, <i>heavy javelin of the
				Gauls;</i> Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαισός</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαῖσον</span> (syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolo, sarissa, sparus, lancea),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 3, 4, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 8, 8, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 36, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 6, 5</span></i>; Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 555, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8,
				662</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Hipp. 111</span></i>; cf.: gaesum grave
			jaculum, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 99</span></i> Müll. <i>N. cr.</i>—In poets the weapon of the
			Africans, <i><span class="en">Sil. 2, 444</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">of the Greeks,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 64</span></i>
			.</div>
